{
  "case_id": "2021-20-1775",
  "document_hash": "a7f771ea39dcae175c445be76ec9fbcdb845f2c24d905d7ba3f6826c521fe804",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Gen. Mark Brnovich",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1775",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7f771ea39dcae175c445be76ec9fbcdb845f2c24d905d7ba3f6826c521fe804",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7f771ea39dc-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BRNOVICH: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The Ninth Circuit's refusal to let Arizona and other states intervene to defend the public charge rule capped an unprecedented effort by the United States to unlawfully disregard a prior administration's rule."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Gen. Mark Brnovich",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1775",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7f771ea39dcae175c445be76ec9fbcdb845f2c24d905d7ba3f6826c521fe804",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7f771ea39dc-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Arizona has a protectable interest because the rule saved the states collectively more than a billion dollars per year."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1775",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7f771ea39dcae175c445be76ec9fbcdb845f2c24d905d7ba3f6826c521fe804",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7f771ea39dc-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Would you explain why you have standing to challenge the Ninth Circuit's preliminary injunction in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1775",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7f771ea39dcae175c445be76ec9fbcdb845f2c24d905d7ba3f6826c521fe804",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7f771ea39dc-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How important is the APA to your argument? What if this were a statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1775",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7f771ea39dcae175c445be76ec9fbcdb845f2c24d905d7ba3f6826c521fe804",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7f771ea39dc-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So this isn't driven entirely by your inability to participate in notice-and-comment and the administration's circumvention of notice-and-comment in your view?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1775",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7f771ea39dcae175c445be76ec9fbcdb845f2c24d905d7ba3f6826c521fe804",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7f771ea39dc-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How important to your argument is it that we already had granted cert on this issue? Does that matter?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1775",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7f771ea39dcae175c445be76ec9fbcdb845f2c24d905d7ba3f6826c521fe804",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7f771ea39dc-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, why is that so?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Fletcher",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1775",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7f771ea39dcae175c445be76ec9fbcdb845f2c24d905d7ba3f6826c521fe804",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7f771ea39dc-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FLETCHER: So, Justice Alito, there's a lot packed into the question that I hope we get to come back to, but I -- I want to sort of get right to the point. I think the first thing to think about when stepping back and looking at the entirety of this situation is that this is not a circumvention of notice-and-comment regulation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Fletcher",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1775",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7f771ea39dcae175c445be76ec9fbcdb845f2c24d905d7ba3f6826c521fe804",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7f771ea39dc-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FLETCHER: So let me take that question on its terms and then, hopefully, come back to some of the premises later. I think, if you have that concern, the solution is not changing the rules of intervention. It's not letting the states come in and make it impossible for the government to acquiesce in adverse decisions, as you suggested the other side's approach would."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1775",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7f771ea39dcae175c445be76ec9fbcdb845f2c24d905d7ba3f6826c521fe804",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7f771ea39dc-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: That -- that's my understanding too. I -- I think it's odd to think about notice-and-comment for repeal after an acquiescence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1775",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7f771ea39dcae175c445be76ec9fbcdb845f2c24d905d7ba3f6826c521fe804",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7f771ea39dc-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Okay. So why isn't it -- why is it wrong for them to intervene to try to Munsingwear the adverse decisions?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1775",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7f771ea39dcae175c445be76ec9fbcdb845f2c24d905d7ba3f6826c521fe804",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7f771ea39dc-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Can we talk about the Munsingwear here? It's Munsingwear of what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1775",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a7f771ea39dcae175c445be76ec9fbcdb845f2c24d905d7ba3f6826c521fe804",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a7f771ea39dc-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Okay."
    },
